    "direct": {
      "decision": false,
      "old": "§1. Tax imposed (d) Married individuals filing separate returns There is hereby imposed on the taxable income of every married individual (as defined in section 7703) who does not make a single return jointly with his spouse, a tax determined in accordance with the following: \n\n    (i) 15% of taxable income if the taxable income is not over $18,450;\n\n    (ii) $2,767.50, plus 28% of the excess over $18,450 if the taxable income is over $18,450 but not over $44,575;\n\n    (iii) $10,082.50, plus 31% of the excess over $44,575 if the taxable income is over $44,575 but not over $70,000;\n\n    (iv) $17,964.25, plus 36% of the excess over $70,000 if the taxable income is over $70,000 but not over $125,000;\n\n    (v) $37,764.25, plus 39.6% of the excess over $125,000 if the taxable income is over $125,000",
      "new": "Replace §1. Tax imposed (d) Married individuals filing separate returns with §1. Tax imposed (a) Married individuals filing joint returns and surviving spouses (i.e., compute tax under surviving-spouse brackets)."
